    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records show very low plasma exposure after oral dosing in humans: abiraterone acetate Cmax 54.67 pg/mL and AUCt/AUCinf about 460/386 pg·h/mL (C36, C39, C34, C41, C37); pachymic acid Cmax 36.3–91.0 pg/mL after 2.5–7.5 g rikkunshito (C32, C33, C30, C31, C35, C38, C40). These are consistent with poor oral absorption/exposure for structurally related terpenoid acids/prodrugs, though they lack IV comparators and are not direct F values.",
      "card_ids": ["C30","C31","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40","C41"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 intestinal absorption/permeability records are mostly formulation solubility in excipients (C42, C49, C45, C51, C43, C44, C47, C50, C46), enteric-release behavior (C52), a PAMPA value for ginsenoside Rg1 (C48), and progesterone aqueous solubility (C53). They do not provide query-specific absorption or permeability evidence and do not overturn the low prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49","C50","C51","C52","C53"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The single high absolute F for withaferin A in rats (87%, C16) is species- and formulation-specific and conflicts with the human poor outcome (C10); it does not provide affirmative evidence for F >= 20% in the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C16","C10"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49","C50","C51","C52","C53"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific intestinal permeability or aqueous solubility data are available; L4 records are for other terpenoids/steroids and mostly in excipients or formulations.",
    "L3 exposure records lack IV comparators and dose-normalized AUC, so very low pg/mL Cmax/AUC is indirect rather than direct F evidence.",
    "Structural similarity to low-bioavailability contexts is qualitative; exact scaffold and functional-group match is not established.",
    "Species and formulation differences, such as withaferin A 87% in rats versus poor in humans, create uncertainty.",
    "No query-specific first-pass metabolism or gut-wall efflux data are available."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains low; L4 does not provide query-specific intestinal absorption/permeability evidence and does not change the prior low decision supported by L1/L2 direct low/poor F outcomes and L3 very low oral exposure. No affirmative evidence supports F >= 20%."
}

